  "stuck_reasons": {
    "A6-emitter-off-register": "A6 validator gate (D4 re-pass with all markers) cannot be cleared within A6's narrow unlock scope (IGenARM64.cpp + asm_funcs + android_runtime_full.cpp). Real-engineering deliverables landed: X19 trampoline save (69b8651b4), 6 off-register helpers fixed, skip-flag dodge fully removed. 52 unique CGOs link before the remaining display.gc NULL fn-ptr BLR \u2014 diagnosed in detail in .autoport/reports/A6-attempt-4-blocker.md. The residual bug needs klink/kscheme runtime fixes + qemu reproduction infrastructure \u2014 scope transitions to A7-emitter-unit-tests-and-qemu-reproduction. Attempt 3 tried a fault-recovery dodge (9ff94b36f) which the supervisor reverted (8f1b4b07e) and validator hardened against.",
    "A8-qemu-repro-and-displaygc-fix": "A8 delivered qemu repro infrastructure + comprehensive root-cause analysis (.autoport/reports/A8-displaygc-root-cause.md): the display.gc NULL fn-ptr BLR is rooted in CodeGenerator::do_goal_function_arm64 emitting NOPs for spill load/store ops. Fix requires unlocking CodeGenerator.cpp which A8's narrow scope didn't have. claude attempt 5 wrote A6-attempt-5-blocker.md with the exact pseudocode for the fix. Scope transitions to A9-codegen-spill-ops (narrow CodeGenerator.cpp::do_goal_function_arm64 unlock for the spill ops).",
    "A9-codegen-spill-ops": "A9 spill-ops landed (59fa70ac4, 0e446973e) and unblocked 16 additional CGOs (45\u219261 link finishes). Next-layer bug surfaced: caller's save area corrupted across GOAL\u2192GOAL BLR. Documented in A9-attempt-1-next-blocker.md. Fix needs IR.cpp narrow unlock \u2014 transitions to A10-callee-save-area.",
    "A17-idiv-emitter-spill": "Same failure fingerprint '3afd18938cb6' has recurred 3 attempts in a row. The agent is no longer learning from validator feedback \u2014 halting to preserve token quota.",
    "A18-type-method-zero-bind": "A18 attempt-4 honest-exited with disassembly-level evidence of TWO arm64 goalc codegen bugs that exceed A18's lock scope (no goalc/* unlocks): (1) X12 regalloc clobber across BLR in dead-pool-heap.get-process \u2014 find-gap-by-size clobbers X12 which held `this`, leading to garbage-receiver dispatch SIGILL; (2) systematic field-offset off-by-4 in arm64 emit \u2014 LDR/STR of basic-relative offsets encode (real-4) instead of real (e.g. (-> this first-gap) at object offset 52 emits LDR Wt,[Xn,#0x30] = 48). A18 attempt-4 shipped the X12-preserve wrappers (workaround, not fix) which proved bug 1 by changing the crash mode from BLR-to-ee_base to BLR-to-stack. See .autoport/reports/A18-attempt-4-next-blocker.md. A19 unlocks goalc/regalloc/Allocator_v2.cpp + goalc/emitter/IGenARM64.cpp to land both fixes together.",
    "A19-goalc-arm64-codegen-fixes": "A19 attempt-1 landed the X12 regalloc fix solidly (IGenARM64::call_r64 now saves X12 via STP/LDP X12,X23 pair; qemu boot crash mode shifted BLR-ee_base \u2192 BLR-stack-address per A18 attempt-4's prediction) but proved with 8 encoder unit tests that the field-offset off-by-4 (Bug 2) is NOT in IGenARM64.cpp's imm12-encoding helpers. The bug must live upstream in the locked compiler layer \u2014 most likely goalc/compiler/IR.cpp::IR_LoadConstOffset::do_codegen_arm64, goalc/compiler/Val.cpp's get_constant_offset_and_base or MemoryDerefVal::to_reg, or goalc/compiler/compilation/Type.cpp's MemoryOffsetConstantVal construction. See .autoport/reports/A19-attempt-1-next-blocker.md for the disproof + A20 unlock recommendation. The supervisor's check 9 (KERNEL.CGO LDR-at-offset-0x34 byte pattern) also had a byte-index bug (data[i+2] vs data[i+1]) which is fixed in A20's validator. A19 X12 deliverable stays in HEAD (commit 3c9574b9f) as a real partial fix; A20 picks up Bug 2 with the compiler unlock.",
    "A20-goalc-arm64-field-offset": "A20 attempt-1 honest-exited via OG_OFFSET_TRACE diag (added to goalc/compiler/IR.cpp:1440/1471/1524/1555, all 4 codegen paths) which produced 196,128 trace lines per backend with zero-line diff after `arch=` strip, and KERNEL.CGO byte-scan at align mod-4=2 confirming 15 instances each of LDR Wt[X16,#48] and [X16,#52]. The A18-attempt-4 off-by-4 hypothesis is falsified: arm64 emit is correct (X16 holds host(user_pointer), not host(start_of_alloc) \u2014 so [X16+48] reads structural offset 52 = first-gap, as intended). A18 attempt-4's disasm interpretation was wrong, not the emitter. See .autoport/reports/A20-attempt-1-next-blocker.md for the four candidate hypotheses for the actual 216-link-finish ceiling: H1 second regalloc surface (weak per supervisor reality-check), H2 X16 corruption in IR_FunctionCall::do_codegen_arm64, H3 klink LDR-literal imm19 NOPs (81 warnings in qemu log), H4 AAPCS arg-shuffle gap in kscheme.cpp::call_goal. Supervisor authored A21 (diagnostic phase) to discriminate via env-gated trace patches in linux_arm64_main.cpp, klink.cpp, Allocator_v2.cpp, kscheme.cpp. A20's diag patch in IR.cpp stays in HEAD as the canonical offset-divergence detector for future phases. A19's X12 fix preserved."
  },
